          "end": 194,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:1",
          "start": 55
        },
        "quote": "(1) Work-site utility vehicles may be operated upon the public highways, streets, roads and alleys within the corporate limits of the City.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.120 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "b8753e59-b1fc-5332-b3f0-9ac66e9f5a20",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 662,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:2",
          "start": 195
        },
        "quote": "(2) “Work-site utility vehicle” means any motor vehicle which is not less than 48 inches in width, has an overall length, including the bumper, of not more than 135 inches, has an unladen weight, including fuel and fluids, of more than 800 pounds and is equipped with four or more low pressure tires, a steering wheel and bench or bucket type seating allowing at least two people to sit side by side, and may be equipped with a bed or cargo box for hauling materials.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.120 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "a9507778-bf84-5c2a-83c6-77d392fab468",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1201,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:3",
          "start": 663
        },
        "quote": "(3) It shall be unlawful to operate any work-site utility vehicle on any public highway, street, road or alley unless such vehicle shall comply with the equipment requirements under the provisions of Article 17, Chapter 8 of the Kansas Statutes Annotated. However, work-site utility vehicles complying with the provisions of Article 17, Chapter 8, need not be registered pursuant to Article 1, Chapter 8 of the Kansas Statutes Annotated to operate on the public highways, streets, roads and alleys within the corporate limits of the City.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.120 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "f07deb0e-aff1-5639-b73a-69f7afb3b635",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1408,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:4",
          "start": 1202
        },
        "quote": "(4) Every person operating a work-site utility vehicle on the public highways, streets, roads and alleys of the City shall be subject to all of the duties applicable to a driver of a vehicle imposed by law.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.120 block 5",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 5,
          "component_id": "951ffa94-32d2-511f-b514-4f99fca5e26d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1625,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:5",
          "start": 1409
        },
        "quote": "(5) It shall be unlawful for any person to operate a work-site utility vehicle in any manner which violates the provisions in this section. A violation of this section shall be deemed an ordinance traffic infraction.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:5#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.120 block 6",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 6,
          "component_id": "efa0055f-af27-5b00-bd48-8dfcd20f762e",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1971,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:6",
          "start": 1626
        },
        "quote": "(b) Operation of Work-Site Utility Vehicles – Valid Driver’s License Required – Penalty. It shall be unlawful for any person to operate a work-site utility vehicle on any public highway, street, road or alley within the corporate limits of the City unless such person has a valid driver’s license. (Ord. 18973 § 1, 10-9-07. Code 1995 § 142-195.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.120:block:6#text",
